cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Bio Arcade in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
title: "Bio Arcade: six single-file browser games teaching biomedical concepts"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-16
authors:
  - family-names: Dhusia
    given-names: Kalyani
    affiliation: "University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences; Arkansas INBRE Data Science Core"
keywords:
  - science education
  - gamification
  - molecular biology
  - pharmacology
  - immunology
  - undergraduate training
abstract: >-
  Six self-contained, mobile-first browser games, each teaching one biomedical
  concept through a flashcard -> gameplay -> quiz loop in which the game
  mechanic models the concept itself: transcription (Polymerase Runner),
  translation (Ribosome Snake), protein folding (Fold-Tris), phagocytosis and
  opsonization (Phagocyte Patrol), pharmacokinetics (Drug Flight), and
  antibiotic mechanism and resistance (Lysis Lab). Developed under Arkansas
  INBRE, supported by NIH NIGMS grant P20 GM103429.
